 ## Overview
-This method accelerates volume rendering by using RTX-accelerated ray tracing to skip empty space. It constructs a bounding volume hierarchy (BVH) over the boundary surface between active and inactive macrocells, rather than over all active regions, to determine ray integration intervals. It differs from [Triangulated Active Brick Boundary Mesh for Space Skipping](1426-triangulated-active-brick-boundary-mesh-for-space-skipping.md) by explicitly leveraging hardware-accelerated BVH traversal and triangle intersection via OptiX/OWL to replace costly software intersection tests, and from Ganter and Manzke's method by replacing the BVH over active brick regions with a BVH over only the boundary, resulting in lower depth complexity and fewer rays [S1].
